			"id": 12,
			"options": {
				"content": "### Error-forensics workflow\n\n1. Find an `api.request.failed` row and inspect its native trace context or `runtime_trace_id`.\n2. Put that value in `traceFilter` to isolate Task state, snapshot, usage and API events in Loki.\n3. Put the same exact 32-character value in `traceId` to render the Tempo waterfall.\n4. The failed `task.turn` segment ends with failure; the continuation segment starts under the same trace without fabricating a new Task turn.\n\nThe Dashboard does not configure datasource correlations. Configure Tempo Trace-to-logs and Loki derived fields separately if you want one-click navigation. Raw prompts, responses, task snapshot content and credentials are not exported. A missing durable-snapshot field means the snapshot had not successfully persisted when the error was observed; missing is not zero or success.",
				"mode": "markdown"
			},
			"pluginVersion": "10.0.0",
			"title": "How to Reconstruct an Error",
			"type": "text"
		}
	],
